; The player-facing UI face: the pixel kit, with a glyph-coverage fallback behind it.
;
; WHY THIS RESOURCE EXISTS. `manasoul_ui.tres` used to name the pixel TTF directly, and
; that kit is ASCII-only -- it has no em dash, no ellipsis, none of the shape glyphs the
; combat interaction readout draws. Every one of them rendered as a missing-glyph box.
; A `Font` carries its own `fallbacks`, so the fix is one resource naming both faces
; rather than a fallback set at each of the dozen call sites that build text.
;
; THE PIXEL KIT STAYS THE PRIMARY FACE. A fallback is consulted only for codepoints the
; base font does not have, so every character that reads correctly today is untouched;
; what changes is the ones that were boxes. The fallback's weight does not match the
; pixel kit and cannot -- that is the accepted trade in
; `UI-FONT-MISSING-EM-DASH-GLYPH-2026-09-22`. Nothing rendering a codepoint box is the
; part that could not ship.
;
; NOT `allow_system_fallback`. The importer already sets it on the pixel kit, and it is
; why this never showed up on a desktop run: the OS supplies the glyph there. The web
; export has no system font to reach, and web is where the tester walks, so a vendored
; fallback is the only one that is true on every platform.
[gd_resource type="FontVariation" load_steps=3 format=3]

